[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Reusable Zero-Heap Mock Flight Instrument Simulation Framework

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-SIM-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Zero-Heap CRTP MockInstrumentBase Harness and Mode FSM
STATEMENT: >>>
The mock instrument framework shall provide a freestanding, zero-heap, zero-vtable CRTP base class MockInstrumentBase implementing a deterministic instrument mode state machine (Off, Boot, Standby, Safe, Science, Calibration, Fault), standard command dispatch, cadence stepping, and packed InstrumentHousekeeping telemetry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A reusable CRTP harness lets mission teams instantiate realistic mock instruments in tens of lines of C++20 while obeying the exact same Class B zero-heap and stack safety budgets as flight software.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: instruments/include/strata/instruments/mock_instrument.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-SIM-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Deterministic Thermal/Power Physics ODE and SCSR RegisterTransport Bank
STATEMENT: >>>
The mock instrument framework shall include a deterministic 1st-order thermal and electrical power physics model (thermal capacitance, radiative sink, heater PWM, mode dissipation, bus voltage/current) synchronized with an SCSR-compatible InstrumentRegisterBlock satisfying strata::RegisterTransport with RO, RW, and RW1C latched fault registers.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Coupling physical thermal/power dynamics to a genuine RegisterTransport MMIO bank allows unmodified flight drivers and FDIR monitors to exercise realistic closed-loop hardware behavior in SIL.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: instruments/include/strata/instruments/mock_instrument.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-MW-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-SIM-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Deterministic Fault Injection Engine and Zero-Copy Science Frame Producer
STATEMENT: >>>
The mock instrument framework shall provide a time-scheduled and on-demand FaultInjector supporting ThermalRunaway, RegisterSeuBitFlip, FrameCrcCorrupt, DmaStall, WatchdogFreeze, PowerBrownout, OverCurrent, and SensorSaturation, alongside deterministic seeded synthetic science frame generation emitting CRC-32C-verified frames directly into zero-copy FramePool slots.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deterministic anomaly injection and reproducible zero-copy science frame production enable automated regression testing of FDIR isolation, data pipelines, and ground limits without physical flight sensors.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: instruments/include/strata/instruments/mock_instrument.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-MW-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-SIM-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Reference Multi-Instrument Mock Implementations
STATEMENT: >>>
The mock instrument framework shall provide at least two concrete reference instruments built on MockInstrumentBase—HyperspectralImagerMock (VNIR/SWIR pushbroom radiometric cube generator with thermal dark current and point-target PSF) and FluxgateMagnetometerMock (tri-axial orbital dipole field synthesizer with calibration coil pulses)—verifying multi-instrument reuse.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Concrete reference instruments prove framework ergonomics across distinct payload physics domains and serve as ready-to-run templates for mission payloads.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: instruments/include/strata/instruments/reference_instruments.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SIM-001

[[/SECTION]]
